    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56699" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κερᾰμ-ῐδόω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make a roof as of shields</i> to protect the soldiers
			(the Roman <i>testudo</i>), <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάκος</span>
			, Hsch.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάκε᾽ ὤμοισι κλίναντες</span>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be roofed</i> or <i>coped with tiles</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεραμιδουμένη . . ἡ οἰκία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					246a28
				</span></i>
			 (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεραμουμένη</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				19
			</span></i> codd.).</div>
